From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 07:50:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/11] pushdown: EMERGENCE-Next protocol N1, weak-site
 corroboration (opt-in, research only)

pushdown.weak_corroborating_sites (optional, 0..10, absent = 0) lets up to that
many sites that confirm with fewer than k records (the <k bucket they already
send) stand in for missing k-record sites, only beside at least one k-record
site. Weak sites add nothing to roots, reporters, support or freshness. A pack
without the key keeps its bytes, config hash and the shipped gate (R0); a pack
with it is a different pack hash, so N1 results can never be read as R0.

Motivation (dev seeds 0-5, offline evidence model): 54 of 240 Gold patterns have
one site with >= k records and a second site with 1..k-1, and are unreachable
under R0 for that reason alone; the same class holds 20 of 300 decoys.

tests/mycelic/test_pushdown_n1.py: R0 unchanged without the key; N1 supports
1 k-site + 1 weak site; never all-weak; weak adds no roots; contributing refute
still contests; the cap holds; out-of-range refused.

